public static int countPeaks(int[][] grid) {
    int count = 0;
    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
        for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
            int v = grid[r][c];
            boolean peak = true;
            if (r > 0 && grid[r - 1][c] >= v) {
                peak = false;
            }
            if (r < grid.length - 1 && grid[r + 1][c] >= v) {
                peak = false;
            }
            if (c > 0 && grid[r][c - 1] >= v) {
                peak = false;
            }
            if (c < grid[r].length - 1 && grid[r][c + 1] >= v) {
                peak = false;
            }
            if (peak) {
                count++;
            }
        }
    }
    return count;
}
```

Each neighbor check is guarded by a bounds test, and short-circuit evaluation ensures the out-of-range index is never accessed. A cell counts as a peak only if no existing neighbor is greater than or equal to it.
